>
>This is how I've done it so far:
>I'll always try to raise my pet first, many times I've had large cat
>when I got killed. I avoid leveling, even if I'm not going for
>protection run. 

  That keeps your Hp nice and low so you can die in one turn.  Not good.


Hide behind your pet.  Help your pet by throwing rocks, darts, etc at tough
monsters.

  Elbereth early and often!  (In addition to survival it exercises wisdom.)
  Bravely run away!
  Throw rocks.
  Do NOT be burdened.  I don't care how much it hurts.  Your main concerns
are armor and weapons.  Dump other stuff by the downstairs before
descending (So monsters won't pick it up.)

  Early gamebreakers for wizards:  
  - GoPower. +6 damage per hit & Expert thrown daggers are devastating.
    The also give +3 to hit.  GoP are like GoDex pre-enchanted to +3 AND
    give a monster damage bonus.
  - Magicbane!  +5 damage bonus, curse resistance, 100% chance of 
    semi-permanant Elbereth (ideal for leaving an item on.)
  - Speed boots, wand of speed monster, or spell of haste self.  (Note that
    the spell can be cast "off-line")
  - Jumping boots are awesome!  Throw and jump,  throw and jump.  (Be 
    careful of the nutrition cost.)
  - One or two highly enchanted pieces of armor.  Since you'll be checking
all body armor, helms, boots, gloves and shields you'll have an excellent
chance of this.  I've found both +4 elven shield and elven mithril.  I wore
them (in different games).




>I'll take notes: what turn I prayed last, what levels
>had store, what levels had vault, shop, fountains, sinks, where are
