  That's all strategy.  Tactics are what you need early on.  Get those down
and they'll get you through the whole game.

  Forget the fun stuff early on.  Later (much MUCH later) you can be an
unstoppable spell casting machine.  Early on you scrabble through every
non-cursed piece of armor you find hoping to scrape up another point of AC.
That can keep you alive long enough to dumpster-dive for more armor.
Lather, rinse, repeat.

  Note that there's a break point at AC:-1 where the damage you take starts
getting reduced.
 
"I'd just read some old Rob Ellwood posts on forgetting spellcasting,
identifying and enchanting until later. I tried it, and what do you
know!" - Milton Pope, YAAP


  Point two:

  Find daggers.  Throw daggers early and often.  Get to Expert dagger
skill.   (If you find GoP you're golden.  You'll do more damage throwing
expert daggers than you would with Grayswandir.)  Get your strength up at
Sokoban for the strength damage bonus.  Magicbane is the wizards guaranteed
first divine gift and uses dagger skill.  It combined with thrown daggers
will do more damage than any other artifact weapon except the Longbow of
Diana.  



